target/

# Cargo layers a project-local .cargo/ config on top of $CARGO_HOME, and a
# `[registry] token` placed there is consumed as a live credential (`cargo
# logout` reports a token present with only this file supplying it), so this is
# where a crates.io token would land if someone put it beside the manifest;
# keep it unstageable (`cargo login` writes $CARGO_HOME/credentials.toml
# instead, which is where a token belongs). Anchored to the crate root: only
# the directory Cargo reads for this crate, so a nested .cargo path stays
# visible instead of being silently hidden. Cargo also consults ancestor
# directories, which this crate-local pattern does not reach.
/.cargo/
